      "height": 1401,
      "desc": "<p>IAA Frankfurt 2019\n</p>\nCupra, Seat's performance brand, launched the Tavascan Concept at the 2019 Frankfurt Motor Show. It is an electric crossover based on VW's MEB with two motors, one integrated on the front axle, and the second at the rear, which provide a combined 306 PS of power to all four wheels. The concept houses a 77 kWh lithium-ion battery pack, which should ensure a driving range of up to 450 km."
